{
  "description": "Cases for the link attribute data-doan-goto=\"<frame id>\". Read by Go (canvas parser, doan check, link groups) and by TypeScript (link groups; later the injected prototype script and the export, which run the html in a DOM). A frame can play when its data-doan-frame id is not empty, no other frame outside <template> has the same id, the id is at most 200 UTF-16 units and its data-doan-prototype mark is valid. placements: a body fragment with what a parser must report outside <template>: frames lists every data-doan-frame element in document order with its raw mark (null when absent); gotos lists every data-doan-goto element in document order with its raw value and the ids of the frames that enclose it, outermost first, including the element itself when it is a frame (a repeated attribute counts only its first value); codes lists the doan check codes about links the fragment must produce, in doan check output order (by code, then innermost enclosing frame, then value); groups lists the link groups. Each link gets at most one target code, judged in order: an empty value or no frame with that id is goto_target_not_found; two or more frames with it is goto_target_shared; one frame whose id is longer than 200 UTF-16 units, or whose mark is missing or invalid, is goto_target_not_prototype. A link with no playable frame among its enclosing frames (including none at all) is also goto_outside_prototype. Values are compared exactly, with no trimming, case folding or Unicode normalization. Link groups: the nodes are the playable frames; each link adds an edge from every playable frame enclosing it to its target when the target can play; a group is a connected set of nodes ignoring direction, its frames in document order, the groups ordered by their first frame. groups: frames and gotos given directly, without html, with the groups they make; frames may leave out frames that cannot play without changing the result. Frames and links inside <template> do not count.",
